         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Quipu on the Yupana\n\nIn this game you will do what the ancient Inca counters did: read the value recorded on the quipu and set that same value on the Yupana. This way you practice reading a number in one system and writing it in another.\n\nFirst, look at the highlighted cord and count its knots; that is the number to read. Then set that number on the Yupana: the bottom row for units, the next row for tens, the row above for hundreds. Tap a square to add a mark; tap it again to remove it. A row with no marks means zero. When both numbers match, the game marks the cord as done.",
